people have been in we fight we dare we  and that my friends is how a revolution  dies if you're a fan of the hunger games  then you know that the four blockbuster  films dealt with some heavy dark and at  more than one time  heartbreaking subject matter so you'd  think that the set would be just as  serious  right well not exactly by all accounts  the hunger games set was known to be a  dynamic playful and cheerful  place despite the dark dystopian  realities of pan m  today we're bringing you the best behind  the scenes moments of this  wickedly talented set including which  tributes pulled off the best pranks  who gave josh hutcherson a bad  concussion and why jennifer lawrence is  according to liam hemsworth somehow the  best and  also the worst actor to work with on set  my smile is so ingenuine people are  going to think that i hate it  despite being love interest on screen  jennifer lawrence and josh hutcherson  were nothing but  absolute pals off screen by all accounts  fellow actors producers and  other personnel could not help but  mention how despite their character's  serious and dramatic storylines these  two could not stop joking around with  each other up until the camera started  rolling  you'd think that the director and his  team would be super annoyed with two  kids fooling around on set  but these two were anything but  unprofessional as soon as the director  yelled  tracking with the three year difference  between the two jennifer and josh  clearly had a big sister little brother  vibe while filming the hunger games  movies  watch these behind the scenes outtakes  of the two chasing and  pushing each other between takes and  don't for a second think that these  feelings expressed by josh weren't  mutual  in this outtake jennifer is literally  pushing him around like a big sister  with a little brother  when you consider how close these two  were it's easy to understand why these  two had such an electric on-screen  chemistry  not to mention seeing these two stars  have fun on the job must have inspired  others on set to not take their job  too seriously one of the most intense  scenes of the four movies is when josh's  character starts to go into a manic in  the mockingjay  on-screen peta looks like he's inches  away from taking away katniss's life  but in real life apparently the scene  was extremely difficult to take without  one or  the other bursting into laughter  watch this hilarious outtake of jennifer  and josh pretending to be cats between  takes to cut the tension of an  otherwise dark and violent scene and  then maybe  we have a shot of being friends  according to sources the hunger games  set was a major prank war between actors  not surprisingly jennifer is probably  the one who started it all when she  accidentally gave josh a minor  concussion while training for a combat  scene on set i kicked him in the head  by accident apparently the only fitting  way josh thought he could get even with  his co-star was to sneak glimmers body  double  into jen's trailer the dummy thing had  me for a little bit listen to these  snippets  on how the prank went down he put a dead  dummy on my toilet holding toilet paper  and scared me  so when she opened up her bathroom to go  to the bathroom she saw a  rotting human being the prank scared jen  so much that there's a circulating rumor  that she even peed her pants with how  terrified she was  sources tell me that she actually peed  her pants i i didn't see it for fact  this just goes to show that you  shouldn't mess with either of these  young actors unless you're ready to be  injured or  downright petrified i just like to keep  a set fun  speaking of pranks other actors took it  upon themselves to put the prank and  joke's queen jennifer in her place  actor jeffrey wright who plays bt in  mockingjay famously gifted his young  co-star a beautiful tiffany box only to  find it full of live crickets  since she opened it in her trailer  jennifer was reported to have spent  weeks trying to get them all out won't  be replicated very easily  jennifer's other co-star liam hemsworth  has also said that working on set was an  absolute blast to the point where it  didn't feel like  work but of course the two being best  friends offset  found it awkward to muster up that  intimate energy for an  on-screen kiss in an interview the actor  revealed that the most awkward scenes to  shoot on set were  any kissing scenes with his co-star  anytime i had to kiss jennifer was  pretty uncomfortable  but don't get it twisted it had nothing  to do with the fact that they weren't  professionals  rather it was because jennifer would  choose specifically what she would eat  for lunch  right before they locked lips she'd be  like yeah i had tuna i had garlic and i  didn't brush my teeth  outside of the katniss peta and gale  love triangle jennifer  also had great relationships with the  other actors on set  one of our favorite on and off screen  dynamics is between jen and the youngest  actor on set  amanda stenberg who played roo jennifer  was really she was great to work with  their chemistry on screen was  absolutely electric and from these  outtakes we can see why  channeling her big sister energy to the  youngest actor on this set  makes us feel all warm and tingly inside  their stuff who wouldn't be crazy  fans will not forget the epic and  unforgettable scene in which katniss is  having her last conversation with roo  after she died protecting the tribute  from district 13.  and while this scene had audiences  everywhere tearing up this tribute says  that apparently jen had this crazy habit  of telling hilarious and inappropriate  jokes right before the director yells  action hey remind me to tell you this  really funny fart joke when this is over  action oh my god although she may look  innocent and harmless amanda was amongst  the most deviant pranksters on the set  of the first hunger games film  alongside another tribute jacqueline  emerson also known as fox face  madeline jackie those two are like the  dynamic duo of pranks okay  this dynamic duo even left a signature  on a posted note every time they pulled  off a prank  their signature prank was stealing the  other actors clothes or even putting  them in the refrigerator  like a note on my mirror that's like  wear your pants jack you'll never find  them  probably the most epic prank pulled off  by these young actresses  involved high school girls a stalker  scare jack quaid who played marvel in  the first film  and alexander ludwig who played cato  because the tributes were shooting off  location they all bunked up in a hotel  close by  so naturally amanda and jaclyn pulled  off some major pranks on their fellow  actors  because that's what you do when you're  hanging out with all of your friends  this prank got so intense that  apparently jack really thought he had a  group of fan girl stalkers on his tail  of course once he found out that this  was all staged he knew  exactly who was behind this epic prank  i battled them it was i i can see the  war  by now you've probably realized that  although they were out to kill each  other in the first flick the actors who  played the tributes in real life  actually liked each other at the end of  every filming day the gang would hang  out  have dance parties and even eat sushi  just check out this clip of the crew  playing ninja between takes on location  no i totally got you it's adventure  singing in the van  and just being silly teens on set  goddamn so hungry  elizabeth banks who plays effie trinket  in the films has by all means the  wackiest  and most performative wardrobe on the  hunger games set  and while we thought she would have  loved dressing to the nines throughout  the films apparently her outfits  prevented her from being candid and  letting loose because of how heavy and  campy they were  i'm stuck in this in this all day long  there's no  question that pan am fashion is  avant-garde to say the least  and while elizabeth banks or effie was  used to it jennifer expressed that it  was difficult for her at times to  channel this feminine part of herself  check out this behind-the-scenes outtake  of jen expressing how she  actually had a nightmare about being in  a big dress in front of a room full of  people  i had this dream that i was in this  ridiculous dress in front of hundreds of  people i don't know  and i just spin around like an idiot  we'll never forget that first scene when  all the tributes are in their arena  it's arguably one of the most dramatic  and intense scenes of the whole movie  and with good reason each person needed  to fight each other to the death for a  chance to get some of the best survival  gear in order to get the best chance of  winning the games  while the scene was beautifully  choreographed what we don't see is how  hot it was that day when the actors were  shooting that famous clip  shout out to juliana for making these  coats so hot shooting on location is  always tricky business and so to combat  the heat jennifer apparently spent much  of her time between takes with her pants  around her ankles  and just having my pants around my  ankles outside i was like i don't even  care anymore  i don't care there's no question that  the hunger games film put amanda on the  map  her role in the first film completely  catapulted her career  you may have recognized her from the big  blockbuster hit the hate u give  but that doesn't mean she has forgotten  her roots and where it all started  in an interview with jimmy fallon on the  tonight show amanda revealed that  jennifer lawrence was a mentor to her  on the set of the hunger games in many  ways  aside from mentoring the young actress  she also very practically taught amanda  how to pee in the woods  what did you learn from jennifer  lawrence um she taught me how to pee in  the woods  so what's your favorite outtake or  behind the scenes blooper  would you have liked to 